; Vendored err_trace (see README.md). The sources are the submodule's own, so
; they are copied rather than duplicated, and the enclosing asm/dune marks this
; tree `vendored_dirs`: dune then suppresses warnings here and leaves it out of
; `@fmt`, which keeps the copy verifiable against the pinned submodule commit.
;
; The stanza lives in its own directory rather than in the submodule because a
; submodule is a foreign checkout - nothing may be written inside it - and
; because ../dune marks that checkout `data_only_dirs`, so a dune file placed
; there would not be read anyway.
;
; `wrapped false` is upstream's own setting and is load-bearing: it is what
; makes the module `Err` rather than `Err_trace.Err`, which is the name the
; whole codebase uses.
;
; Melange mode lives in melange/vendor/err_trace, which copy_files these same
; sources; the two stanzas share this library's name and are made mutually
; exclusive by ASM_MELANGE, because dune cannot make `modes` conditional.

(copy_files#
 (files ../err_trace/src/err.ml))

(copy_files#
 (files ../err_trace/src/err.mli))

(library
 (name err_trace)
 (wrapped false)
 (modes byte native)
 (enabled_if
  (<> %{env:ASM_MELANGE=false} true)))
